#{[17592186489272 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186489061 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489272 #edb/ref 1069 "q-96933" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489272 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489272 #edb/ref 1071 "The table below gives the values of ${Φ}^{-1}(p)$ for different values of $p,$ where $p=Φ(z)$ is the cumulative distribution function for the standard normal distribution. Find the value of $z$ such that $P(Z\\le z)=0.995.$\n\n| $p$ | $\\,0.900\\,$ | $\\,0.950\\,$ | $\\,0.975\\,$ | $\\,0.990\\,$ | $\\,0.995\\,$ | $\\,0.999\\,$ | $\\,0.9995\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| ${Φ}^{-1}(p)$ | $\\,1.2816\\,$ | $\\,1.6449\\,$ | $\\,1.9600\\,$ | $\\,2.3263\\,$ | $\\,2.5758\\,$ | $\\,3.0902\\,$ | $\\,3.2905\\,$ |" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489272 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "d124118c-140f-52f2-b4ac-16dbd784c35b" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489272 #edb/ref 1074 "First, we express the given information in terms of $Φ:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(Z\\le z) & =0.995 \\\\ Φ(z) & =0.995\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we are looking for the value of $z$ such that\n\n$$\nz={Φ}^{-1}(0.995).\n$$\n\nWe look for the column in the table that corresponds to $p=0.995,$ and we find that\n\n$$\np=0.995\\,⇒\\,{Φ}^{-1}(p)=2.5758.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\nz={Φ}^{-1}(0.995)=2.5758.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489273 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186489100 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489273 #edb/ref 1069 "q-328465" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489273 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489273 #edb/ref 1071 "The table below gives the values of ${Φ}^{-1}(p)$ for different values of $p,$ where $p=Φ(z)$ is the cumulative distribution function for the standard normal distribution. Find the value of $z$ such that $P(Z\\le z)=0.20.$ Use the table below and do not round your answer.\n\n| $\\,p\\,$ | $0.10$ | $0.15$ | $0.20$ | $0.25$ | $0.30$ | $0.35$ | $0.40$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| ${Φ}^{-1}(p)$ | $\\,-1.2816\\,$ | $\\,-1.0364\\,$ | $\\,-0.8416\\,$ | $\\,-0.6745\\,$ | $\\,-0.5244\\,$ | $\\,-0.3853\\,$ | $\\,-0.2533\\,$ |\n\n$z=$\n{{field-1}}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489273 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "d5e93823-c39c-538e-930e-c856e7a48401" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489273 #edb/ref 1074 "First, we express the given information in terms of $Φ:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(Z\\le z) & =0.20 \\\\ Φ(z) & =0.20\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we are looking for the value of $z$ such that\n\n$$\nz={Φ}^{-1}(0.20).\n$$\n\nWe look for the column in the table that corresponds to $p=0.20,$ and we find that\n\n$$\np=0.20\\,⇒\\,{Φ}^{-1}(p)=-0.8416.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\nz={Φ}^{-1}(0.20)=-0.8416.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489278 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186489102 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489278 #edb/ref 1069 "q-96960" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489278 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489278 #edb/ref 1071 "The table below gives the values of ${Φ}^{-1}(p)$ for different values of $p,$ where $p=Φ(z)$ is the cumulative distribution function for the standard normal distribution. Find the value of $z$ such that $P(Z\\le z)=0.015.$\n\n| $\\,p\\,$ | $0.965$ | $0.970$ | $0.975$ | $0.980$ | $0.985$ | $0.990$ | $0.995$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| ${Φ}^{-1}(p)$ | $\\,1.8119\\,$ | $\\,1.8808\\,$ | $\\,1.9600\\,$ | $\\,2.0537\\,$ | $\\,2.1701\\,$ | $\\,2.3263\\,$ | $\\,2.5758\\,$ |" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489278 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "e2cf6287-aa23-5f4b-8eb1-c626aabdf157" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489278 #edb/ref 1074 "From the table, notice that\n\n$$\nP(Z\\le 2.1701)=0.985.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\nP(Z\\ge 2.1701)=1-0.985=0.015.\n$$\n\nBy the symmetry of the standard normal distribution, we have\n\n$$\nΦ(-2.1701)=0.015.\n$$\n\n![](images/47/47a123a730cf175bea1d1887ffdc5a9feb3e1d8f07208c28a9f893a9a1688005.png)\n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Φ(-2.1701) & =0.015 \\\\ P(Z\\le -2.1701) & =0.015.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the required value of $z$ is $-2.1701.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417]}
